-- chem/sos.cub — a lower end as a checked identity. For an operator H on modes 0..k−1 and N particles, the level is at
-- least λ when H − λ = Σ_k c_k·B_k†B_k + (N̂ − N)·X with every c_k ≥ 0: the squares are positive and N̂ − N vanishes on
-- N particles. `fa-cert` decides the identity by normal form (chem/fermi.cub), over any coefficient ring; the signs
-- of the weights c_k are the one thing it leaves, as numbers when the ring is the rationals. The certificate is
-- found anywhere; this is the whole of its check, and its size does not depend on N.
import "fermi.hypercubical"

